                <pb facs="0392" n="286" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg286"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Blaine asks whether the promotor fiscal in one of the five points made by
                    him, viz, the third, says that the evidence of the officers and crew of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi> has been thrown out because conflicting,
                    as Capt. Evans of the <hi rendition="#italic">Yorktown</hi> telegraphs.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
